msgid "Dshot capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:92
#: a7bcf85d331f4ff6baf0f944fa053fe5
msgid "All motor/servo outputs are Dshot and PWM capable. Outputs 1/2, and 5/6 are Bi-Directional DSHOT capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:94
#: 640c63c95b884792a607a0d6d0fd5cae
msgid "The output groups are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:96
#: 343262ed60d64fc4af7e953676881a4d
msgid "1/2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:97
#: 69d5d439cb6c4d84be3a8aae14f6fd6a
msgid "3/4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:98
#: e988969718dd4026bd22e06ff4cac46c
msgid "5/6/7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:99
#: 64016f58beec4a5da68eeff963e0e79a
msgid "8/9/10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:100
#: 382caf42a4ca49149fadfbff5339e419
msgid "11/12(LED)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:102
#: 72a1b6f25c51446597875ce6c50ae304
msgid "output 12 is marked as \"LED\" and defaulted for serial led protocol. If output 11 is to be used, then :ref:`SERVO12_FUNCTION<SERVO12_FUNCTION>` must be changed to \"0\" or some other normal servo/motor function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:105
#: 7d1d04e257fc40078af340e2afeb852e
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:107
#: dc76839dd3224d03b8ad28ceef769c09
msgid "USART2 is defaulted for RC input. The SBUS pins are passed through  an inverter to RX2 (UART2 RX). SBUS/FPort should be connected to an SBUS input, However, FPort, when connected in this manner, can provide RC but without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:109
#: e7e7ef46832145c992a919de53e7c8f2
msgid "Other RC protocols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:111
#: 9f35752db8ea43889445cd7f0db7a134
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:113
#: cdfa6e321ec74a9cab36e7b0326f7b89
msgid "DSM/SRXL connects to the RX6  pin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:115
#: fc1671bc446c4e2eb407a429abb7b525
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX2 and RX2 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:117
#: 914db4b79e4a4bc4857d4b03da731d3d
msgid "CRSF/ELRS also requires a TX2 connection, in addition to RX2, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:119
#: d9ec7e462f0e49979f3ba03b0e60c33a
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX2 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL2_OPTIONS<SERIAL2_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:121
#: 00a1d1ce7e4d48778f59765960623991
msgid "the 5v pin above the SBUS pin is powered when USB is connected. All other 5V pins are only powered when battery is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:124
#: 67ee393a3de44b7085d65dd9e965e24a
msgid "RF Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:126
#: aaa8fe8e92744b6783518417142db8af
msgid "A BLERF module is integrated on board and connected to USART1, but is not currently supported by ArduPilot Ground Control stations. This module is powered off by default, but power to it can be controlled by setting up a relay function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-atomrcf405-navi-deluxe.rst:128
#: 8bf6fdc49d5e45c5b70a802e61a9775e
msgid "Enable a relay via ``RELAYx_EN`` and set its  ``RELAYx_PIN`` to “81” to control the  switching. Then select an RC channel for control (Chx) and set its ``RCx_OPTION`` to the appropriate Relay (1-6) that you had set its pin parameter above. ``RELAY 2`` is assigned by default to this GPIO pin, but would need :reF:`RELAY2_FUNCTION<RELAY2_FUNCTION>` set to \"1\" to enable it."
msgstr ""

